# v4.4.0 — line-ending normalization. Every text file in the repo is
# stored with LF; checkouts on Windows don't rewrite them.
#
# Historically this repo had no .gitattributes, so Windows editors
# auto-converted LF -> CRLF on save and every `git status` /
# `git diff` was drowned in "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings.
# Fixed in v4.4.0 per the attestqa reply dated 2026-10-11; a
# follow-up "chore: normalize line endings" commit runs
# `git add --renormalize .` so the whole tree lands at LF.
#
# Platform-specific scripts stay as CRLF where the OS requires it
# (PowerShell / Windows batch).

* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be normalized.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.vsix binary
*.tgz  binary
*.zip  binary
*.onnx binary
